!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-namespace-type-leaving-a-facet-open-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    A value of a namespace type is a map from its `key_type` to its `value_type`, which the type pins by
    composition. `keyed` pins its keys and leaves `value_type` open, so it describes no map, and it is not
    abstract, so nothing else will pin it: the meta layer declaring it fails to load. Declared `abstract`, it
    would be a base for namespace types that pin the rest.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
